  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tobacco Free Cities: implementation research with city governments in Bangladesh, Pakistan and Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Obj 1: To explore strategies that promote tobacco smoke-free cities in six Asian cities. 

Obj 2: To evaluate the implementation of smoke-free laws and enforcement strategies. 

Obj 3: To generate insights to enable effective adaptation of evidence-based strategies to promote tobacco smoke-free cities in LMICs.

Obj 4: To build capacities amongst researchers and implementers in study countries to conduct tobacco-related implementation research in complex urban contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal will address this implementation research challenge. the Overall Aim is to work with city actors (city governments and civil society) and the public in two cities (1 mega, 1 secondary) each in Bangladesh, Pakistan, and Vietnam to critically examine the implementation of strategies for enforcing smoke-free laws with a view to generate insights for effective implementation and scale-up of these strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
